Insertion Sort in Python

Insertion Sort is one of those algorithms that looks almost too simple at first. 
Then you realize the idea behind it appears in many places in everyday life.

Think about arranging playing cards in your hand. 
You pick one card, compare it with the cards already arranged, shift the larger cards, and insert the new card into its correct position.
That is essentially Insertion Sort.

For each element starting from the second element:

•Store the current element as key.

•Compare key with the elements before it.

•If an element is greater than key, shift it one position to the right.

•Continue comparing until the correct position is found.

•Insert key into that position.

•Repeat until the complete list is sorted.
